    {
      "id": "cb13-l2",
      "title": "READ … AT END",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "To go through a whole file, READ until there are no more records. AT END runs when the file is used up; NOT AT END runs for every record that was read.",
        "The usual pattern: an 88 level END-OF-FILE on a flag, and PERFORM UNTIL END-OF-FILE with a READ inside.",
        "Reading again after the end is an error, so the loop must stop as soon as AT END happens."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.",
          "       PROGRAM-ID. ALLCUST.",
          "       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.",
          "       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.",
          "       FILE-CONTROL.",
          "           SELECT CUST-FILE ASSIGN TO CUSTOMERS.",
          "       DATA DIVISION.",
          "       FILE SECTION.",
          "       FD CUST-FILE.",
          "       01 CUST-REC.",
          "          05 CUST-NO      PIC 9(5).",
          "          05 CUST-NAME    PIC X(12).",
          "          05 CUST-CITY    PIC X(10).",
          "          05 CUST-BAL     PIC 9(5)V99.",
          "       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.",
          "       01 EOF-FLAG       PIC X VALUE \"N\".",
          "          88 END-OF-FILE VALUE \"Y\".",
          "       01 COUNTER        PIC 99 VALUE ZERO.",
          "       PROCEDURE DIVISION.",
          "           OPEN INPUT CUST-FILE.",
          "           PERFORM UNTIL END-OF-FILE",
          "               READ CUST-FILE",
          "                   AT END SET END-OF-FILE TO TRUE",
          "                   NOT AT END",
          "                       ADD 1 TO COUNTER",
          "                       DISPLAY CUST-NO \" \" CUST-NAME",
          "               END-READ",
          "           END-PERFORM.",
          "           CLOSE CUST-FILE.",
          "           DISPLAY COUNTER \" CUSTOMERS\".",
          "           STOP RUN."
        ],
        "output": [
          "00007 GRACE HOPPER",
          "00042 ADA LOVELACE",
          "01959 JOHN BACKUS ",
          "02024 LINUS T.    ",
          "04 CUSTOMERS"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "cb13-l2-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "When does AT END run?",
          "options": [
            "When READ finds no more records",
            "After every READ",
            "When the file is opened",
            "At STOP RUN"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "It's how the program knows the file is finished."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb13-l2-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does NOT AT END run?",
          "options": [
            "The statements for each record that was read",
            "The statements at the end",
            "Nothing",
            "The next READ"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Every successful READ."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb13-l2-e3",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Mark the end of the file.",
          "code": [
            "               AT END SET END-OF-FILE TO ___"
          ],
          "options": [
            "TRUE",
            "YES",
            "1",
            "END"
          ],
          "answer": "TRUE",
          "explanation": "SET … TO TRUE for the 88 level."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb13-l2-e4",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "How many records does the CUSTOMERS file have, judging by the example?",
          "options": [
            "4",
            "3",
            "5",
            "7"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "The counter shows it."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb13-l2-e5",
          "type": "find_bug",
          "prompt": "This job stops with a READ error. Which line is wrong?",
          "code": [
            "       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.",
            "       PROGRAM-ID. TOOMANY.",
            "       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.",
            "       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.",
            "       FILE-CONTROL.",
            "           SELECT CUST-FILE ASSIGN TO CUSTOMERS.",
            "       DATA DIVISION.",
            "       FILE SECTION.",
            "       FD CUST-FILE.",
            "       01 CUST-REC.",
            "          05 CUST-NO      PIC 9(5).",
            "          05 CUST-NAME    PIC X(12).",
            "          05 CUST-CITY    PIC X(10).",
            "          05 CUST-BAL     PIC 9(5)V99.",
            "       PROCEDURE DIVISION.",
            "           OPEN INPUT CUST-FILE.",
            "           PERFORM 10 TIMES",
            "               READ CUST-FILE",
            "                   AT END DISPLAY \"NO MORE\"",
            "               END-READ",
            "           END-PERFORM.",
            "           STOP RUN."
          ],
          "answer": 16,
          "explanation": "The file has only 4 records, but the loop keeps reading after the end. Loop UNTIL END-OF-FILE instead."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb13-l2-e6",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What closes a READ with AT END clauses?",
          "options": [
            "END-READ",
            "END-FILE",
            "CLOSE",
            "A period only"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "END-READ, like END-IF."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cb13-l3",
      "title": "WRITE",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "OPEN OUTPUT creates a new, empty file (an old one with that name is replaced). WRITE puts the record into it as the next line. You WRITE the record, not the file: WRITE BACKUP-REC.",
        "WRITE … FROM copies a WORKING-STORAGE field into the record first: WRITE BACKUP-REC FROM CUST-REC.",
        "The example copies every customer with more than 1,000 dollars into a new file RICH, then reads RICH back."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.",
          "       PROGRAM-ID. RICHJOB.",
          "       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.",
          "       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.",
          "       FILE-CONTROL.",
          "           SELECT CUST-FILE ASSIGN TO CUSTOMERS.",
          "           SELECT RICH-FILE ASSIGN TO RICH.",
          "       DATA DIVISION.",
          "       FILE SECTION.",
          "       FD CUST-FILE.",
          "       01 CUST-REC.",
          "          05 CUST-NO      PIC 9(5).",
          "          05 CUST-NAME    PIC X(12).",
          "          05 CUST-CITY    PIC X(10).",
          "          05 CUST-BAL     PIC 9(5)V99.",
          "       FD RICH-FILE.",
          "       01 RICH-REC      PIC X(34).",
          "       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.",
          "       01 EOF-FLAG       PIC X VALUE \"N\".",
          "          88 END-OF-FILE VALUE \"Y\".",
          "       PROCEDURE DIVISION.",
          "       MAIN.",
          "           OPEN INPUT CUST-FILE OUTPUT RICH-FILE.",
          "           PERFORM UNTIL END-OF-FILE",
          "               READ CUST-FILE",
          "                   AT END SET END-OF-FILE TO TRUE",
          "                   NOT AT END",
          "                       IF CUST-BAL > 1000",
          "                           WRITE RICH-REC FROM CUST-REC",
          "                       END-IF",
          "               END-READ",
          "           END-PERFORM.",
          "           CLOSE CUST-FILE RICH-FILE.",
          "           MOVE \"N\" TO EOF-FLAG.",
          "           OPEN INPUT RICH-FILE.",
          "           PERFORM UNTIL END-OF-FILE",
          "               READ RICH-FILE",
          "                   AT END SET END-OF-FILE TO TRUE",
          "                   NOT AT END DISPLAY \"IN RICH: \" RICH-REC",
          "               END-READ",
          "           END-PERFORM.",
          "           CLOSE RICH-FILE.",
          "           STOP RUN."
        ],
        "output": [
          "IN RICH: 00007GRACE HOPPERNEW YORK  0250000",
          "IN RICH: 00042ADA LOVELACELONDON    0181536"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "cb13-l3-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does OPEN OUTPUT do to an existing file with that name?",
          "options": [
            "Replaces it with a new, empty file",
            "Adds to its end",
            "Reads it",
            "Nothing"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Use OPEN EXTEND to add to the end instead."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb13-l3-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "WRITE needs:",
          "options": [
            "The record's name, like WRITE RICH-REC",
            "The file's name, like WRITE RICH-FILE",
            "A DISPLAY",
            "OPEN INPUT"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "A classic saying: read a file, write a record."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb13-l3-e3",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Copy the customer record into the backup record and write it.",
          "code": [
            "           WRITE BACKUP-REC ___ CUST-REC."
          ],
          "options": [
            "FROM",
            "TO",
            "INTO",
            "USING"
          ],
          "answer": "FROM",
          "explanation": "WRITE … FROM …."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb13-l3-e4",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "How many customers end up in RICH?",
